  "interpretation": "<p><br></p><table><thead><tr><th><div>Total Protein Level</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>Below Normal Range</div></td><td><div>Hypoproteinemia (low total protein levels) may be indicative of malnutrition, liver disease, kidney disease, gastrointestinal malabsorption, or certain inflammatory conditions. Further evaluation is needed to determine the underlying cause and appropriate treatment.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Above Normal Range</div></td><td><div>Hyperproteinemia (high total protein levels) can occur in conditions such as dehydration, chronic inflammation, certain infections, or certain blood disorders. Clinical correlation is necessary to determine the underlying cause and management approach.</div></td></tr></tbody></table>",
